    "restoration_notes": "Excellent small native fruit species for diversified agroforestry systems. Produces fruit throughout the year, providing continuous food for households and wildlife. Its adaptability allows use in home gardens, living fences, and restoration of degraded farm boundaries. The compact size makes it ideal for community restoration projects where space is limited. Requires minimal management beyond pruning and adapts to a wide range of growing conditions. Within FYNOS AI, pitanga is recommended as a complementary fruit species for diversified, multi-strata restoration landscapes emphasizing food security and biodiversity."
